      "reasoning": "  **GG! I won!** 🎉\n\
\n\
My opponent is at **-3 life**! The combat damage went through perfectly:\n\
\n\
- Spirebluff Canal dealt **4 damage** (unblocked)\n\
- Mountain dealt **2 damage** (unblocked)\n\
- Total: **6 damage** to their 3 life = **-3 life**\n\
\n\
The game state shows they've died with an empty library and graveyard containing their creatures. \n\
\n\
Fascinating how this game played out:\n\
1. **Lesson synergy** - I used Combustion Technique early, which fueled later damage\n\
2. **Adaptive creatures** - Stormchaser's Talent and Spirebluff Canal became massive threats\n\
3. **Tight racing** - We were both at single digits, but my 9 total attackers vs their 2 blockers meant lethal got through\n\
\n\
The edge case on High Noon (each player can only cast one spell per turn) made sequencing critical, but my creature-heavy deck was well-positioned against it! \n\
\n\
Library's power prevails indeed! 📚⚔️",
